  "acting": {
    "comment": "K9 performance layer. leadMs: eyes arrive first, head next, body last (eye-lead, replaces eye lag). asym: right side gets an extra delay and gain jitter so no two sides are mirrors. snapMs: attack for fast beats (1-3 frames). releaseMs: settle back to neutral. Escalation ladder for reactions: small (default) -> medium (streak 3) -> large (rare).",
    "enabled": true,
    "leadMs": 45,
    "lead": [
      "eyes",
      "head",
      "body"
    ],
    "asym": {
      "delayMs": [
        8,
        45
      ],
      "gainJitter": 0.18
    },
    "snapMs": 40,
    "holdFrames": [
      2,
      8
    ],
    "releaseMs": 340,
    "settleEasing": "cubic-bezier(.34,1.56,.64,1)",
    "escalation": {
      "small": 1,
      "medium": 3,
      "largeEveryN": 7
    },
    "brows": true,
    "browsComment": "vector brows (data-feature=brows in owl_p2.svg); shown only when acting.brows is true and the page flag ?brows!=0; joints browL/browR, pivot at brow centre lower edge; channels rot (tilt, deg) and y (raise, px)",
    "wink": {
      "ms": 180,
      "otherSquint": 0.22,
      "pupilLeanPx": 1.5,
      "headTiltDeg": 4,
      "comment": "one lid closes fully, the other squints 22 pct; open pupil leans to the winking side; head tilts 4 deg (overlap)"
    },
    "escalationComment": "consumed by rig.escalate(channel): small most of the time, medium every 3rd, large every 7th; channels: flight, celebrate",
    "intent": {
      "comment": "K9.3 intent: look before you leap. Before every flight the pupils snap toward the target (eyes first), the head turns after headLagMs (P1 Zangemeister-Stark 1982: normal eye-head latency 40-50 ms), then the body crouches after bodyLagMs (P2 Fang 2015: a fixation-saccade cycle is >= 200 ms). Budgets are declared here and measured by sandbox/intent_proof.py; ?intent=0 disables for A/B.",
      "enabled": true,
      "gazeSnapMs": [
        40,
        70
      ],
      "gazeFractionOfDart": 0.85,
      "headLagMs": [
        40,
        50
      ],
      "headDeg": 5,
      "headMs": 220,
      "bodyLagMs": [
        200,
        280
      ],
      "landRecentreMs": 100,
      "settleDegTarget": 0.5,
      "settleWithinMs": 400,
      "budget": {
        "preTakeoffMs": [
          350,
          600
        ],
        "gazeDirectionMatch": 0.6,
        "asymMinPx": 0.3
      },
      "measureNote": "settleDegTarget and the crouch onset are measured on the ADDED layers (intent head layer, squash layer keyframes), not on the computed transform: the idle breath is a permanent +-1 deg head tilt / +-2.5 pct body scale by design (rig.idle), so an absolute reading can never settle below it. Found and documented 2026-09-26 (K9.3-3); nothing hidden.",
      "bodyLagNote": "was [120,200]: measured pre-takeoff 293-382 ms fell short of the declared 350-600 (bodyLag + crouch hold 150-250). 200-280 = the body waits one fixation-saccade cycle (P2 Fang 2015: >= 200 ms) -> 350-530 ms total.",
      "asymNote": "L/R pupil jitter is now min budget.asymMinPx .. gaze.dart.asymPx apart by construction (one flight measured 0.27 px with independent jitters)."
    },
    "performances": {
      "comment": "K9.4 owner-vision performances. Each channel escalates through rig.escalate(channel) with acting.escalation (small small medium small small medium large). Structure per P6 (Webster 2005): anticipation squash -> extreme stretch -> settle. Budgets declared 2026-09-27 before code (PROGRESS K9.4 RESEARCH); measured by perf_proof.py. ?perf=0 falls back to the pre-K9.4 clips.",
      "enabled": true,
      "triumph": {
        "comment": "jump of joy; medium lifts the apex and adds stars; large adds a 360 root roll at the apex (level before landing, |rot| < 2 deg) and hearts",
        "jumpPx": 52,
        "anticipateMs": [
